/	P?S/8 REWIND AND UNLOAD ROUTINES

/	COPYRIGHT (C) 1975-1989, CHARLES LASNER ASSOCIATES; 1990-2014, CLA SYSTEMS.

/	LAST EDIT: 19-MAY-2014 CJL.

/	TAKEN FROM A 1978 P?S/8 SYSTEM TAPE IMAGE [KNOWN TO NOT BE A FINAL RELEASE].

/	THIS SMALL ROUTINE IS THE P?S/8 KEYBOARD MONITOR AND IMBEDDED EDITOR CODING
/	TO HANDLE CONTROL-R AND CONTROL-T CHARACTERS WHICH CAN BE TYPED DURING THE
/	ENTRY OF ALL FORMS OF COMMANDS OR TEXT.

/	CONTROL-R IS MEANT TO BE USED TO REWIND THE CURRENT SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER
/	DRIVE UNIT [ASSUMING THE HARDWARE IS SOME FORM OF TAPE DEVICE].  SIMILARLY,
/	CONTROL-T IS MEANT TO BE USED TO UNLOAD THE SAME DEVICE.  NOT ALL SYSTEMS
/	SUPPORT THESE COMMANDS EQUALLY; ON SOME SYSTEMS THE COMMANDS ARE VIRTUALLY
/	INTERCHANGEABLE; ON OTHER SYSTEMS BOTH COMMANDS ARE IGNORED.

/	EACH SPECIFIC HARDWARE-DEPENDENT RELEASE OF P?S/8 SUPPORTS A CUSTOM VERSION OF
/	THIS CODE TAILORED FOR THE SYSTEM DEVICE HARDWARE OF THAT PARTICULAR SYSTEM
/	[IF THE HARDWARE SUPPORTS THESE COMMANDS AT ALL].  THE ACTIONS TAKEN ARE
/	PARTICULAR TO THE HARDWARE CONFIGURATION.

/	THE CODE DECRIBED HERE IS FOR THE TC01/TC08 DECTAPE CONTROLLER.  ANY MIX OF
/	TU55 AND TU56 DRIVES IS SUPPORTED; HOWEVER, THE EXACT ACTIONS TAKEN ARE
/	DEPENDENT ON THE DRIVE TYPE:

/	WHEN CONTROL-R IS TYPED, THE CURRENT TAPE DRIVE UNIT IS REWOUND TOWARDS THE
/	REVERSE END ZONE.  CONTROL IS IMMEDIATELY RETURNED TO THE KEYBOARD MONITOR TO
/	ALLOW ADDITIONAL KEYBOARD INPUT WHILE THE TAPE IS REWINDING.  WHEN THE TAPE
/	ENTERS THE END ZONE, THE CONTROLLER DETECTS THIS AS AN END ERROR, AND STOPS
/	THE TAPE AUTOMATICALLY.

/	THIS ALLOWS THE USER TO TYPE ADDITIONAL COMMANDS DURING THE TAPE REWIND
/	OPERATION TAKING ADVANTAGE OF OVERLAPPED OPERATION.  THIS COULD INCLUDE
/	ENTERING AN EXECUTION-CLASS COMMAND KNOWN TO REQUIRE ACCESS TO BLOCKS NEAR THE
/	PHYSICAL BEGINNING OF THE TAPE; SHOULD THE COMMAND REQUIRES ACCESS TO THE
/	DECTAPE DRIVE, THE REWIND OPERATION IS CANCELLED BY THE CALL TO THE SYSTEM
/	DEVICE HANDLER.

/	WHEN CONTROL-T IS TYPED, THE CURRENT TAPE DRIVE IS REWOUND; HOWEVER, THE
/	ROUTINE WAITS FOR THE END ERROR.  ADDITIONAL OPERATIONS ARE PERFORMED TO FORCE
/	THE TAPE OFF THE TAKE-UP REEL.  WHAT HAPPENS NEXT DEPENDS ON THE DRIVE TYPE:

/	1) IF THE SELECTED DRIVE IS A TU55, ADDITIONAL COMMANDS ARE ISSUED TO MODIFY
/	   TAPE DIRECTION AND MOTION BITS FORCING THE TAPE REELS TO LOCK.

/	2) IF THE SELECTED DRIVE IS A TU56 [WHICH LACKS MECHANICAL BRAKING], THE TAPE
/	   REELS ROTATE UNCONTROLLABLY UNTIL THE USER RESETS THE DRIVE; THE ADDITIONAL
/	   COMMANDS ARE IGNORED.

/	AFTER THE UNLOAD OPERATION HAS COMPLETED, CONTROL IS RETURNED TO THE KEYBOARD
/	MONITOR TO ALLOW ADDITIONAL KEYBOARD INPUT; NO COMMAND OVERLAP OCCURS
/	P?S/8 SYSTEM DEFINITIONS.

	CURUNIT=0000			/LATEST LOGICAL DRIVE UNIT IN BITS[9-11]
	KBDCHR=	0100			/LATEST KEYBOARD INPUT CHARACTER
	KBDLUP=	1216			/KEYBOARD MONITOR INPUT ROUTINE
	L200=	0104			/CONSTANT 0200
	L7756=	0064			/CONSTANT 7756
	L7770=	0040			/CONSTANT 7770
	REWUNLD=1342			/REWIND/UNLOAD ROUTINE LOADS HERE
	RWTEMP=	1305			/AVAILABLE TEMPORARY FOR TIMING LOOP

/	TC01/TC08 DECTAPE DEFINITIONS.

	CA=	7755			/CURRENT ADDRESS REGISTER FOR 3-CYCLE DATA BREAK
	DTCA=	6762			/CLEAR STATUS REGISTER "A"
	DTLA=	6766			/LOAD STATUS REGISTER "A" FROM AC, CLEAR AC
	DTLB=	6774			/AC[6-8] TO BREAK FIELD, CLEAR AC
	DTRA=	6761			/STATUS REGISTER "A" .OR. INTO AC
	DTRB=	6772			/STATUS REGISTER "B" .OR. INTO AC
	DTSF=	6771			/SKIP ON DECTAPE FLAG OR ERROR FLAG SET
	DTXA=	6764			/AC .XOR. INTO STATUS REGISTER "A", CLEAR AC
	WC=	7754			/WORD COUNT REGISTER FOR 3-CYCLE DATA BREAK

/	HISTORICALLY, P?S/8 SYSTEM GENERATION CONSISTS OF PLACING ALL COMPONENTS
/	AFFECTED BY CHOICE OF SYSTEM DEVICE INTO MEMORY AT THE SAME TIME.  THE
/	SPECIFIC CODE PARTICULAR TO THE CHOSEN DEVICE IS THEN OVERLAID OVER THE BASIC
/	ROUTINES TO PRODUCE A CUSTOMIZED SYSTEM.

/	TO CUSTOMIZE P?S/8 IN THE FUTURE, NEW MECHANISMS NEED TO BE DEFINED TO
/	COMPLETELY DEFINE THE SYSTEM SPECIFICS.  SYSTEMS SUCH AS OS/8 MERELY NEED TO
/	DEFINE A SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER; OTHER SYSTEM COMPONENTS SUCH AS THE REWIND AND
/	UNLOAD ROUTINES DO NOT EXIST ELSEWHERE.

/	FOR THE PRESENT, ACCESS TO THE SOURCE CODE IS NEEDED, INCLUDING ALL CODE
/	SPECIFIC TO THE HARDWARE.  IN SOME CASES, THIS WAS PARTIALLY CREATED BY HAND
/	OR TRANSFERRED BY IMAGE COPYING FROM OTHER SYSTEMS THAT SUPPORTED P?S/8 BUT
/	NOT THE CODE SPECIFICS [SUCH AS CREATING TD8E SYSTEMS ON THE TC01/TC08-BASED
/	SYSTEM].

/	THIS FILE WILL BE AN EXAMPLE OF A MODULARIZED APPROACH TO THE CURRENT
/	MECHANISM; FUTURE DESIGNS MAY AGGREGATE ALL RELATED COMPONENTS.
	*REWUNLD			/REWIND/UNLOAD ROUTINE.

REWUNLD,TAD	L7770/[7770]		/SETUP THE MAIN
	DCA	RWTEMP			/TIMEOUT COUNTER.
	TAD	CURUNIT			/GET THE CURRENT LOGICAL DEVICE UNIT BITS.
	CLL RTR;RTR			/MOVE TO AC[0-2].
	TAD	L700/(700)		/ADD REWIND FUNCTION BITS.
	DTLA				/START THE TAPE REWIND.
	TAD	KBDCHR			/GET THE COMMAND CHARACTER.
	TAD	L7756/(-22)		/COMPARE TO CONTROL-R.
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF NOT CONTROL-R.
	JMP	KBDLUP			/GO GET MORE KEYBOARD INPUT.
UNLWAIT,DTSF				/FLAG UP YET?
	SKP				/SKIP THE NEXT IF NOT.
	JMP	REWUNLD			/FLAG IS UP, GO FORCE THE TAPE TO MOVE.

/	THE FLAG ISN'T UP YET, SO WAIT FOR SOME TIME.

	ISZ	KBDCHR			/INNER LOOP: ENOUGH TIMES?
	JMP	UNLWAIT			/NO, KEEP WAITING.
	ISZ	RWTEMP			/WAITED LONG ENOUGH?
	JMP	UNLWAIT			/NO, KEEP GOING.

/	AT THIS POINT, THE DONE FLAG WILL NO LONGER RAISE; THE TAPE MUST HAVE FALLEN
/	OFF THE REEL AND IS SPINNING OUT OF CONTROL.

	TAD	L400/(400)		/GET DIRECTION-CHANGE BIT.
	DTXA				/REVERSE DIRECTION.

/	THE CONTROLLER IS NOW SET TO FORWARD MOTION.  THERE IS NO TAPE MARK DETECTION
/	IN PROGRESS BECAUSE THE TAPE IS OFF THE REELS.  WE NEED TO WAIT TO ALLOW THE
/	COMMAND TO SETTLE BEFORE SENDING ANOTHER COMMAND.

/	THE FOLLOWING EXECUTES AS "AND I 1300".

L700,	700				/CONSTANT 0700.

/	THE FOLLOWING EXECUTES AS "AND I CURUNIT".

L400,	400				/CONSTANT 0400.

/	THE FOLLOWING EXECUTES AS "AND CURUNIT".

	ZBLOCK	0			/EMPTY SPACE RESERVED FOR ALTERNATE CODE.

	TAD	L200/[200]		/GET MOTION BIT.
	DTXA				/STOP THE TAPE, LOCKING THE BRAKES.

/	ALL OF THE FOLLOWING EXECUTE AS "AND CURUNIT".

	ZBLOCK	KBDLUP&7600+177-.	/EMPTY SPACE RESERVED FOR ALTERNATE CODE.

	JMP	KBDLUP			/GO GET MORE KEYBOARD INPUT.
/	SHOULD NOW BE ON THE NEXT PAGE.

	IFNZRO	.&177	<ERROR	.>

/	NOTES:

/	THE USE OF THE CONSTANT 0700 IS ARBITRARY AS BIT[5] [WHICH SETS CONTINUOUS
/	MODE] IS IGNORED IN DECTAPE MOVE COMMANDS.  AS SUCH, 0600 WOULD ALSO WORK AND
/	PERHAPS BE THE MORE LIKELY CHOICE.  OTHER CONSIDERATIONS MAY HAVE INFLUENCED
/	THE DESIGN.

/	THE SPECIFIC USE OF SOME OF THE CONSTANTS AND TEMPORARIES IN THIS CODE COULD
/	BE A SPECIFIC CONSEQUENCE OF OTHER ROUTINES IN THE KEYBOARD MONITOR CODE NOT
/	SHOWN HERE.  [THE BULK OF THE CODE IS KNOWN TO BE EXTREMELY OPTIMIZED FOR
/	MINIMAL CODE SPACE; CONSIDERATIONS DOWN TO THE BIT LEVEL HAVE BEEN MADE FOR
/	MOST ROUTINES.]

/	THE SPECIFIC LENGTH OF THE RESERVED EMPTY SPACE HAS LIKELY CHANGED SLIGHTLY
/	DEPENDING UPON THE RELEASE.  THE SOURCE CODE AUTOMATICALLY ADAPTS AS NECESSARY
/	AS LONG AS THERE IS SUFFICIENT SPACE FOR THE REST OF THE PROGRAM.  [NOTE: IT
/	IS PRESUMED THAT "ZBLOCK 0" IS SUPPORTED AS GENERATING NOTHING; IF THIS IS NOT
/	THE CASE, THE SOURCE CODE NEEDS TO ADD A CONDITIONAL LAYER TO PREVENT ANY
/	UNEXPECTED PROBLEMS.]

	$				/THAT'S ALL, FOLK!

